<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CycloneDDS tuning for the simulation. Matches perseus-v3's middleware so sim
  and robot run the same RMW, and so the perseus-v3 autonomy stack
  (autonomy_bringup localisation.launch.py sim:=true) can subscribe to the
  sim's topics.

  DISCOVERY IS DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE. This file tunes transport sizing only.
  An earlier version bound <Interfaces> to "lo" on the reasoning that the sim is
  one host talking to itself. That broke everything: loopback carries no
  MULTICAST flag (ip link shows <LOOPBACK,UP,LOWER_UP>), so Cyclone had no
  multicast-capable interface and discovery failed outright - `ros2 topic list`
  returned only /parameter_events and /rosout, even between two processes on
  this machine, and the localisation stack saw no sim topics at all.

  The perseus-v3 dev shell sets no CYCLONEDDS_URI, so it runs Cyclone's default
  interface autodetection. This side must do the same or the two never meet.
  Note this is a different job from perseus-v3/config/cyclonedds_autonomy.xml,
  which binds ROAR_DDS_IFACE and lists unicast peers for the multi-machine rover
  LAN; that config is for the robot network, not for talking to the sim.

  What is left is purely about message size. /livox/lidar is 720 x 32 points at
  32 bytes = 737 KB per message at 10 Hz. On stock settings a cloud that big is
  fragmented and roughly half of them are lost: Gazebo published a steady 9.8 Hz
  while ROS subscribers saw ~5.5 Hz with gaps over a second. The IMU, at a few
  hundred bytes, was unaffected at 200 Hz - which is what pointed at size rather
  than load. It matters more here than it looks, because BIEVR-LIO subscribes
  best-effort (qos_reliable: false), so a lost fragment is not retransmitted.

  Both settings are capped by the kernel: SocketReceiveBufferSize cannot exceed
  net.core.rmem_max, 4 MB on this machine. Cyclone warns and continues if it is
  given less, so this is safe to carry to a machine with a smaller limit.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <Internal>
      <!-- Must exceed one 737 KB point cloud; default is far below it. -->
      <SocketReceiveBufferSize min="4MB"/>
      <Watermarks>
        <!-- Default is 500 kB, i.e. smaller than a single cloud, so the
             writer stalls partway through every message. -->
        <WhcHigh>8MB</WhcHigh>
      </Watermarks>
    </Internal>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
